contentText:
LL Cool J has finally explained himself.

The rap legend and actor stopped by 7PM in Brooklyn With Carmelo Anthony , and toward the end of the interview, he was asked by co-host Kazeem Famuyide about the infamous hand gesture he made toward Booker T during an appearance on WWE&#8217;s Smackdown back in the early 2000s.

&#8220;They didn&#8217;t have to tell me. I already knew,&#8221; he said after Melo asked him if the WWE staff told him to create his own signature move. &#8220;I&#8217;m the &#8216;Ax Man.&#8217; It&#8217;s like an executioner that licks his ax before he chops your head off and all that. I was bananas. I was there five minutes, look at that. I just went with the vibe. I&#8217;m vibin&#8217;.&#8221;

He then added that specific move is just the tip of the iceberg in terms of things he has in his repertoire. &#8220;I&#8217;m just nuts, man. Ya man is nuts. I do what I wanna do. I&#8217;ll own it,&#8221; LL continued. &#8220;I&#8217;m crazy, I do all of it on purpose, but I got better sh&#8211; than that in the cut. This is just the start, this ain&#8217;t nothin&#8217;. I&#8217;m wondering where the good stuff is at. That ain&#8217;t nothing, I&#8217;m way past that.&#8221;

For what it&#8217;s worth, he did address the gesture in 2023 after someone on X asked him what it meant. &#8220;It means I’ll lick the blood off my blade after I chop your head off,&#8221; he tweeted . &#8220;Who wants it? Haha.&#8221;

LL was on Smackdown in 2002 to promote his film Rollerball .

